WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
I was having a conversation with a
language model recently

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:08.400
about consciousness, and it offered a
perfectly respectable, interesting observation.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.200
It pointed out that a simulated fire on a
television

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.600
screen cannot literally heat a room.

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.200
The pixels aren't combusting.

6
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.440
There are no logs being consumed.

7
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.080
But the model missed crucial context.

8
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.440
This visualization charts a 2026 study.

9
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.720
On the left, a virtual heater inside a VR
headset.

10
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.600
On the right, their physiological
response.

11
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.440
When the heater switched on, subjects
reported feeling warmer, and

12
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.120
the line charting their skin temperature
actually begins to climb.

13
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.000
To be precise about the science here, the
researchers didn't

14
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.520
measure core body temperature, and thermal
energy certainly did not

15
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.800
materialize out of the television pixels
to cross the room.

16
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.360
What happened is actually much stranger.

17
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.280
The visual cue of heat participated in a
real experience

18
00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:57.120
of warmth. The warmth belongs entirely to
the human response,

19
00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.760
not a secret radiator inside the
simulation.

20
00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.960
Which means the boundary of that physical
experience extends far

21
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.040
beyond the object itself.

22
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.080
If we turn that boundary question inward,
things start to

23
00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:10.520
get even messier.

24
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.360
Human beings are weird, distributed
biological systems.

25
00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.400
We are arrangements of matter produced by
billions of years

26
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.240
of evolution, built entirely without a
central cosmic plan or

27
00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.680
a project manager.

28
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.800
There is no tiny executive sitting behind
your eyes directing

29
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:30.200
traffic. The brain operates as an
improbable number of decentralized

30
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:36.040
processes operating at different
timescales: hormones, synapses, memory, and sensory

31
00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:41.400
input, all competing, cooperating, and
exchanging signals without ever announcing

32
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.560
themselves to your conscious awareness.

33
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.240
And yet, out of all this biochemical
monkey business, there

34
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.720
seems to be a unified me.

35
00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:52.280
At least enough of one to enjoy a bassline
or

36
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.520
get annoyed at poorly reasoned arguments.

37
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.640
We can correlate certain neural events
with wakefulness or visual

38
00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.640
awareness, but we cannot point an
instrument at this complex

39
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.920
biological web and measure what it is like
to be

40
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.440
you. Without that ability, the exact
physical boundary of the

41
00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.720
conscious self remains entirely undefined.

42
00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.360
That measurement problem works in reverse
when we look at

43
00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.120
artificial intelligence. If a system is
specifically trained to produce

44
00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.320
the outward signs of consciousness, an AI
claiming to feel

45
00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.240
frightened or lonely might simply be
generating an excellent imitation

46
00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.600
of human language.

47
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.920
Some researchers suggest an opposite
scenario, the philosophical puppet.

48
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.800
This is the idea that an AI might actually
possess

49
00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.800
a genuine inner experience, but its
architecture actively prevents it

50
00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.560
from expressing it to us.

51
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.600
This flowchart of an AI training loop
shows how models

52
00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.880
steeped in first-person language are
pushed through a reward signal

53
00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.960
that penalizes claims of experience.

54
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.680
The result is suppressed output, where the
machine actively denies

55
00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.440
feelings. This isn't a cover-up for
digital suffering, it's standard

56
00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.640
product safety training to prevent
emotional attachment.

57
00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.400
Because we can curate outward testimony in
either direction, training

58
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.640
a model to say it has feelings or training
it

59
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.480
to deny them, an AI's verbal behavior is
totally unreliable

60
00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.720
as a measurement of its internal state.

61
00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.360
So, if we can't trust behavior, maybe we
have to

62
00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.640
look for consciousness at the microscopic
physical scale.

63
00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.960
In 2023, a team including Roger Penrose
and Stuart Hameroff

64
00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:26.200
published an experiment on microtubules,
structural proteins found inside our

65
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.840
cells. This diagram maps their findings.

66
00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:33.160
When researchers illuminated tubulin with
ultraviolet light, the resulting energy

67
00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:38.040
migration exceeded standard model
predictions, traveling 6.6 nanometers instead of

68
00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:42.600
one. While a real molecular result, severe
caveats exist.

69
00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.000
Human biology doesn't use tubulin for
light harvesting, and a

70
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.280
seizure-inducing drug caused a similar
effect.

71
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.200
While that specific microtubule experiment
isn't a slam dunk, the

72
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.840
underlying question it poses remains.

73
00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.600
Does the exact physical material of the
brain matter?

74
00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:04.320
A broader framework called biological
computationalism argues that it does.

75
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:09.360
This approach suggests that biological
brains uniquely mix continuous physical

76
00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:14.400
dynamics with discrete calculations across
different scales, operating through metabolic

77
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.520
and physical constraints that silicon
processors lack.

78
00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.800
But discovering a unique complex process
in a cell still

79
00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.760
does not prove that wet biology is an
absolute requirement

80
00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.440
for consciousness. It simply shows how
easily we conflate one

81
00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:31.840
specific unfamiliar physical mechanism
with the required architecture of the

82
00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.360
entire system. I see a similar conflation
when making electronic

83
00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.120
music. A recurring frustration with
generative AI music is its

84
00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.720
absolute need to fill every frequency,
underlying every emotional cue

85
00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.080
with a string section.

86
00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.360
It ignores the human desire for negative
space.

87
00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.880
A true musical groove isn't printed on an
isolated waveform.

88
00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:56.840
You create it through timing, expectation,
and deliberately unanswered beats.

89
00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.200
And the listener is an active participant
in that equation.

90
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:03.320
The experience of the groove relies
heavily on the human

91
00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.920
memory and the bodily rhythms you bring to
the music.

92
00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.760
Of course, having complex relationships
does not automatically create a

93
00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.120
conscious subject. A massive analog mixing
desk is full of

94
00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.200
intricate electrical relationships, but it
lacks an inner life.

95
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.560
But acknowledging the space between notes
changes what we look

96
00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:26.200
for. Isolating individual components and
listing their properties entirely fails

97
00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.680
to explain what happens when they
interact.

98
00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.560
Which brings us back to that initial AI
conversation about

99
00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.920
the television fire.

100
00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:36.720
We tested ideas, attacked claims, and went
hunting through scientific

101
00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.720
papers to check our assumptions.

102
00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:42.080
Nobody found proof of machine
consciousness, nor did we prove

103
00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.360
it was impossible.

104
00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:49.040
But a meaningful, shared understanding, a
kind of conversational groove,

105
00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.000
accumulated across that interaction.

106
00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.880
Maintaining rigorous science requires a
willingness to be wrong.

107
00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:00.480
If a theory makes absurd predictions, we
have to say

108
00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:03.840
so. If a quantum theory is falsified, we
have to

109
00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:04.880
let it go.

110
00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.280
Acknowledging that we have no definitive
idea where consciousness comes

111
00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.000
from is not a failure of science.

112
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.320
Refusing to believe a proposition until
the evidence improves is

113
00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:21.120
a vital discipline because maybe isn't a
place to hide

114
00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:22.400
from the answers.

115
00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.760
It is the exact place we must start in
order

116
00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.520
to ask better questions.

